  "description": "This is a Martin ERA 700 Performance IP, a moving-head spot. A rectangular base, probably with a small display and four buttons on its front, carries a U-shaped yoke whose two arms hold the tilt pivot on either side of the head. The head is a rectangular box, 0.46 by 0.76 by 0.31 metres if the units are centimetres, probably with ventilation grilles on both sides and a carrying handle on top. Pan covers 540 degrees and tilt 260 degrees, both DMX-driven, moving the whole head. The front face has one circular lens, about 11.7 units across, set off-centre, with nothing arranged in a grid. One light cell sits behind that lens. Zoom, frost, blades and wheels are DMX functions or nodes without geometry.",
